sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila planitibia detail-tier Turing wavelength (5.13 µm, Holocene 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila planitibia morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila planitibia specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila planitibia; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics a - u + u^2 v, b - u^2 v. | Edwards et al. (2007) document Hawaiian picture-wing patterns. Kambysellis et al. (1995) Current Biology 5:1129 place the picture-wing radiation phylogenetically. Carson (1982) describes the newer-volcano radiation that includes Maui D. planitibia. | Assigned phenomenon scale for this detail variant: 5.13e-06 m (5.1 µm, log10 = -5.290) at geological age 0 Ma.; reconstructed_in_script: Linearized Fourier probe on the real Turing band: Pearson r = 0.99999993 (p = 6.39e-39, RMSE = 7.20e-05) against the discrete dispersion symbol. Interpolated wavelength 5.097 µm versus the 5.13 µm calibration. | Equal-diffusion ablation ratio 45.76. Unstable diffusion ratios d = 12 to 40 give a strictly lengthening wavelength. D_u(117 µm)/D_u(5.13 µm) = 520.16 and D_u(114 µm)/D_u(5.13 µm) = 493.83 at age delta 0 Ma. | Specimen scale bar 111 px = 100 µm. Spiral-band ridge 67.57 µm, Otsu circularity 0.662, radial-spectrum KS = 0.719 versus the rendered field. CV similarity of the 12-frame GIF is 87.6.; transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg kinetics are a generic activator-inhibitor model placed at the assigned 5.13 µm tier. They are not a fitted yellow/ebony circuit for D. planitibia.; does_not_claim: That Edwards, Kambysellis, or Carson measured 5.13 µm, or that the 67.57 µm spiral carrier is that wavelength. | That DOI 10.1073/pnas.92.17.7819 is the Hawaiian Drosophila phylogeny. | A counted foretarsal-cilium spacing, or a signed nanopublication (no local nanopub profile).]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/s0960-9822(95)00229-6>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/hdy.1982.2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0000487> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

